// A constructor name alone is not a constructor. In an expression it is an
// ordinary variable name, so a read with no such variable is the catchable
// UndefinedVariableError (spec/02-syntax.md, enum declaration). In a pattern
// a bare name is never a constructor pattern: it is a binding that matches
// every value (spec/04-semantics.md, match Expression, "Constructor
// patterns").
enum E { A B }

try {
    print A;
} catch (e) {
    print e.kind;
}

print match E.B() { case A => "bound " + str(A) };

var B = "a variable";
print B;

// STATUS: ok
// CHECK: UndefinedVariableError
// CHECK: bound B
// CHECK: a variable
